WEBVTT

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.290
Damn it.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.370
This is what we get for failing to catch him back in Shinjuku.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.380
According to feng shui,
Shibuya's basically a demon gate.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.630
You're pretty superstitious,
despite hating wizards.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.880
Girls are into fortunetelling.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.090
Can you really call yourself a girl?

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.160
Here it comes.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.300
He's not getting away this time!

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.160
Inspector Quinn!

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:36.860
Seriously?!

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.880
Stop the train!

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:58.380
As of 10:37, Otoo Shigeki has been secured.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.890
With your magic sealed,
you're just another human, you son of a bitch.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.900
Get me a wizard barrister.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.390
I won't talk until you do.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.150
Otoo, the Court for Magic
is waiting for you.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.540
According to article 1 of the
magic-prohibition law:

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.640
The punishment for using magic, in commission of a homicide,

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:32.170
as well as the destruction of a railway vehicle,
resulting in several casualties,

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:39.460
causing social unrest
among the city, is very grave.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.930
We hereby sentence
the defendant to death.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.020
H-Help!

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.020
Let's go.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.820
That was as disappointing as usual.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.820
Wizard barristers are seen as villains.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.170
Especially when dealing with a Wud who's also a vicious criminal.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.820
Well, this was the natural outcome.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.430
I'm sure you're pleased, given that it was the recommended ruling.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:37.580
This business wouldn't be worth shit
if he, of all people, had gotten off lightly.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.940
By defending Otoo,
in the face of public opinion,

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.200
does Butterfly stand to gain anything?

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.370
We don't expect any
gain or loss from this job.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.220
By the way, I heard you were getting two newbies in April.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:54.620
I'm surprised you'd know about that.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.130
One of them's been the
talk of our department too.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:05.060
...Cecil...

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.500
Hey, Cecil.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.100
You'll get in trouble if
you don't get up soon.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:14.600
Cecil!

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.620
...I'm pulling off the covers...

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.260
What are you doing, Nana Genie?

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.510
No way!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.160
Nana Genie, you idiot!

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.120
Why didn't you wake me up earlier?!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.040
It's your fault for staying up so late.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.540
But I couldn't sleep because I was so nervous...

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.550
Just hurry up and get ready.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.040
I can still make it.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:45.100
I can still make it.
I can still make it. I can still make it.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.470
I can still make it.
I can still make it. I can still make it.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.220
I think!

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.640
Hurry up.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.140
I can't believe I'm
running late on my first day.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:04:59.650
Only Bicycles Allowed

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.900
I know you don't have any sense of direction,
but where are you going?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.840
I think this is a shortcut.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:08.910
Huh?

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.820
How do you read your name?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.620
And did you see the sign back there?

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.080
I'm sorry, I wasn't paying attention.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.670
Wud

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.670
Sudou Cecil

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.600
She's a wizard.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.170
Huh?

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.380
Mind if we take a look inside your bag?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:34.430
Unless there's a justifiable reason,

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.980
everyone has the right to decline a
search of their personal belongings.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.690
Not to mention you can't do so
without having a search warrant on you.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.980
Good job.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:53.740
Since I have a choice, then there's no reason for
me to show you my bag without a warrant, right?

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:05.260
Public servants never change.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.850
It's not like we have magic in our bags.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.050
And this is exactly why
we need wizard barristers.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.310
A metamoloid.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.310
Come on, Nana Genie!

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.200
Where are we going?

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.070
I've got a good idea.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.950
Leave it to me.

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:35.950
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:35.950
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:42.250
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:42.250
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:57.720
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:57.720
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:01.710
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:01.710
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.020
but in the present?

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.020
erabareta ima

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:07.370
The scales of justice are fragile

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:07.370
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:12.430
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:12.430
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.330
the color of blood

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.330
chi no iro no hana

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.830
I will give all I have

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.830
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.530
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.530
subete wo sasageyou

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.810
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.810
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.660
which I will show the world

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.660
kaze ni hanatte

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.660
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.660
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.330
and look at a new world

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.330
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.980
My love stabs at the cracks

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.980
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.470
of a stagnant fate

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.470
omoi wa nejikonde

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:38.350
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:38.350
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.960
time itself will not stop breathing

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.960
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.720
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.720
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.190
and further destruction?

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.190
nani ga nokoru darou

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.920
I'm sure I can put an end to a thousand nights of doubt

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.920
sou nanajuuokuban no mayoi mo

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:52.060
and to the system of the world

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:52.060
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.730
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.730
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho e

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.970
even if only ashes will remain

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:58.970
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:06.910
She's half Canadian, born in Ontario,
and she's just returned from abroad.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.500
At fifteen, she passed the national bar,

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:14.210
Sword and Scales

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:14.210
Case 1

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:14.360
and at seventeen, she's the youngest wizard barrister ever!

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.260
...She's so smart...

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.770
You can tell she's on a
completely different level.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.410
So she's basically like a
stoic virgin with no time to play.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:25.110
Right?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.400
Just like you, Sori!

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.900
Shut it!

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.910
Why'd she come to our office, though?

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.160
Everyone, listen up!

00:08:38.920 --> 00:08:41.790
I'm going to introduce the
newbie who's starting today.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.550
My name is Hotaru Natsuna.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:51.490
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:53.790
Aw.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:54.930
What?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.760
We also have another
newbie starting today.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.720
She should be here any moment.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.560
Mizuki

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.560
Bank

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:09.480
Hey, w-wait!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.990
Civilians aren't allowed inside!

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:13.990
I'm not a civilian!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.740
I'm a wizard barrister from
Butterfly Law Offices, Sudou Cecil!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.740
...Sudou Cecil...

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.500
Wizard barrister?

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.970
Is that the victim?

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:26.380
The bank robber.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:27.510
Bank robber?

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:29.790
Butterfly is finished.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.130
Yep.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.130
Um, where's the suspect?

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.640
The wizard's right over there.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:41.520
I will be his attorney!

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.850
Huh?

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.600
She's extremely late.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:48.110
She has some nerve,
being late on her first day.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:53.190
I really wanted to introduce
everyone when Sudou arrived.

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.670
I see.

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:58.620
If she's going to be late, though,
then perhaps it's better if you get rid of her?

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:02.370
I don't want to work with someone
who has no idea how society works.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.710
Doesn't hold back, does she?

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:05.620
...Ageha...

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.120
Yes?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:10.630
Assistant Inspector Shizumu,
of the police, is on the line.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:15.850
So, your newbie barrister said she'd
...represent the suspect in today's incident...

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.350
Starting today, I'll call you "Natcchi".

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.270
I'd rather you not.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:17.170
She totally denied me, Sori!

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.390
Newbie?

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.390
How about Hotarin, then?

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:21.520
Please stop giving me
strange nicknames.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.890
Her name was Sudou Cecil.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:28.600
I'm sorry! I'm late!

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:29.810
Oh, there she is!

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:33.820
...Super scary...

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.820
Despite how my face looks,
I am your boss, Chouno Seseri!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.320
I'm Sudou Cecil.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:43.510
Accepting a case as an excuse for your
tardiness isn't how a newbie should act!

00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:44.950
...That wasn't what I intended...

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:49.300
Besides, you're in no position to
offer a defense without any permission!

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:50.530
I'm sorry.

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.840
And look at how you're dressed!

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.840
Doesn't she realize she's a barrister?

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:00.550
In a judge's eye, that probably
...wouldn't be too good...

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.170
Aw! But she's so cute!

00:11:03.170 --> 00:11:05.810
Seventeen and super lovely!

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.290
Wizard barristers don't need idols!

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.810
These are my battle clothes.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.560
Please let me wear them!

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:14.770
You're free to battle in
whatever clothes you'd like.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.900
If you can fight in that,
then it's okay with me.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.850
...A-Ageha...

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:21.580
Now tell me about the
case that you accepted.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.080
Sure!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.730
A Wud robbery gang by the
name of "No Face" attacked a bank.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.240
One of the customers,
Mr. Kohinata Souta, decided to fight back.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.070
He killed one with his magic,

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.130
and was arrested.

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:08.370
Let's get an interview
with Mr. Kohinata, then.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:09.910
You'll be in charge of this, Cecil.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:11.210
Right!

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:15.800
Ageha, you want a newbie
to start casework already?

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:17.500
Of course.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.800
She <i>did acquire the case.</i>

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.360
Sasori, you'll be her advisor.

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.740
I agree with Seseri.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.250
...Is it really a good idea to let a newbie—

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:28.810
Please let me do it!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.100
Well, they say experience
is the best teacher.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:37.820
Yeah. We won't know unless we try.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.320
Good grief!

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.790
Hope your experience sucks.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:41.820
Consider it training.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.530
Thank you very much!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:53.120
Mr. Kohinata, could you
tell us what happened?

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:56.910
You've got to believe us.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.130
We know we can help you.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.710
You seem pretty sure of yourself.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.670
Huh?

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:07.110
You're cute, seventeen, and a barrister.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.930
There's no way you could know how I feel.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:17.940
Do something about your appearance.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:21.030
You don't want to be at a disadvantage from prejudice, do you?

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:23.190
Is that really the problem here?

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:26.200
Yes, but I don't count.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:28.700
Why are you laughing?

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.690
I'm off.

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:36.120
Thanks for your hard work!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.310
Cecilun, how did your first interview go?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.630
I was really nervous.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:45.630
I'm just a paralegal so I can't say much,

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:48.090
but everything is worth experiencing.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.390
Yes!

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:52.550
I hope that I can become a full-fledged
barrister soon, for the sake of our clients.

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:57.440
Is that why you offered a defense without any permission, Sudou?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:59.370
The suspects don't have anyone.

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:04.690
I can't just stand idly by,
knowing how much a barrister can help.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:05.990
That's pretty naïve.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.620
If you think wizard barristers can
save people, then you're highly mistaken.

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.040
Hachimitsu never changes.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:17.370
No, I <i>will save them.</i>

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:23.410
...She's...

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.950
...Sudou Cecil....

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.800
Familiars aren't masseurs!

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:33.120
But my legs are all swollen.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.020
You're pretty tense here!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:37.430
I don't need you to massage that!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.940
Seriously, you're working too much.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.280
I want to become a
professional as soon I can.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.320
No matter what anyone else says.

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.490
You perverted frog!

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:52.490
Oh, my!

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:57.350
Here's the footage of No Face, the robbers,
when they fled the crime scene.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:05.590
After forensics reviewed the evidence, this was identified
as a metamoloid, created by a Wud that controls metal.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:08.790
We're trying to analyze the
small amount of metal in custody,

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:13.420
but as of right now,
we have no more evidence or leads.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:15.490
Quinn, report.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.020
Kohinata remains silent.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.020
...However...

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:22.770
New allegations have arisen.

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:25.940
This is security camera footage
from inside the bank.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:31.570
As you can see, Kohinata has gone in and out of the bank daily for a few weeks now.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:35.820
Kohinata is a former bank employee.

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:39.630
With his knowledge of the bank, we have reason
to believe that Kohinata was an accomplice

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:42.920
that wound up killing a comrade for an unknown reason.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.420
Kohinata is a bank robber?!

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.290
That's how the police see it.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:48.920
The prosecution is heading that way too.

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.250
They have photographic evidence.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.930
At this rate, we're at a disadvantage.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.450
Let's canvass the employees.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.690
They may have some information.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:58.430
Okay!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:03.090
I heard that you got the police
information for Ageha, Baamin.

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.190
Yeah.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.940
I'm glad I could be of help again.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.070
You're a pretty scary receptionist.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:13.450
If you ever need my help,
just let me know.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.240
Bank

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.240
Mizuki

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.740
Butterfly Law Offices Wizard Barrister

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:19.490
You witnessed the incident,
right, Ms. Endou?

00:16:19.490 --> 00:16:22.750
I was scared, so I don't
really remember much.

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:26.470
Mr. Kohinata was a
former coworker, right?

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.250
What kind of person was he?

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:30.650
...W-Well...

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:32.550
Are you done?

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:37.450
We are also victims, and we're busy with
trying to get the bank up and running again.

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:40.070
That was harsh.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:43.050
A former coworker was arrested,
and not only did they not defend him,

00:16:43.050 --> 00:16:45.330
but they treated him like a bad guy.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:49.350
Companies are pretty harsh
against troublemakers.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:53.770
By the way, Cecilcchi,
have you ever been with a guy?

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:56.710
Wh-What are you asking, all of a sudden?!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.080
As you senior coworker,
I order you to tell me.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.410
You're really into that stuff,
aren't you, Sasori?

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:03.170
Yep.

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:04.780
Is that a problem?

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.080
Hold on.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.150
Hello?

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:10.090
Yes, this is Sasori.

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:14.090
Thank you for earlier.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.090
Self-defense?

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:19.150
One of the robbers was about to attack me.

00:17:19.150 --> 00:17:23.570
When Kohinata tried to stop him,
he was attacked instead.

00:17:23.570 --> 00:17:26.850
That's when Kohinata
used magic against him.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:30.360
Why didn't you tell us that earlier?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.590
...Well...

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:36.050
Apparently, she was too afraid
of the manager to tell the police.

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:41.240
She apologizes for not
being able to thank you.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.500
Mr. Kohinata, you were being
harassed at your workplace, right?

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:49.250
...For being a Wud...

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:55.010
But Endou would always
greet me and was nice to me.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:57.390
I'm sure that was enough
to make you happy.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:17:59.640
You can tell?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.350
You like Endou, don't you?

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.420
Oh, really?

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.890
I can sense other people's relationships.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:11.200
You aren't too sharp, are you, Sasori?

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.780
What'd you say, newbie?

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:18.390
Just seeing her every day was enough.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:21.450
That's why, even after quitting,
I kept coming by.

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:26.350
So that explains the security footage that's
now being used as unfavorable evidence against us.

00:18:26.350 --> 00:18:29.620
But since it was self-defense, it'll work out!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.790
...Magic-prohibition law, article 10...

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:36.870
"If magic is used for social justice, then it is not considered a crime."

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:41.220
So if we have your actions acknowledged
as self-defense, we'll have the upper hand.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.100
We'll win this one for sure!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.930
We can't lose with self-defense.

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:53.670
Cecil, what are you doing?

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:54.860
This is an ema.

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:58.420
You write your wish on it, then hang it up.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:02.120
Japan has a lot of customs.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:05.120
Is Cecilun late again?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.870
She's off this morning.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.930
How lucky for her,
considering she's a newbie.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.790
I specifically allowed it.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:15.380
She has something
important to take care of.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.730
How are you doing?

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:47.290
You scared me!

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.410
Let's go take a breather.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:54.230
The cherry blossoms are in full bloom.

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.850
I didn't even notice.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.450
You're working too hard, Cecilun.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.570
Well, you can't stop time.

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.270
I'll have to find a way
to stop it for you, then.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.170
Moyo, do you hear voices or something?

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.140
Don't be so boring, call me Moyoyon!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.190
Okay, Moyoyon.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.940
Hooray!

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:17.460
By the way, you had a half day today. What did you do?

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:20.970
Well... I went to see
a condemned criminal.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:21.650
Huh?

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.650
Please don't tell anyone yet.

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:25.990
Sure,

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:27.670
...but who was this—

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.210
Wh-What?

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:36.190
Give me your wallets.

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.470
How could you use magic
to commit a crime?!

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.960
Cecilun!

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.210
No, no, no!

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:43.010
Get off of me!

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:43.010
Shut up!

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.260
...Wait! If it's money you want...

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.890
<i>Cecil Diaboloid!</i>

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:54.990
Go!

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.750
...Wow...

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.490
There wasn't enough metal,
so it ended up smaller than usual.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.670
What?!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:26.430
It's incomplete too!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.470
You little!

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:35.020
Please turn yourself in.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.150
I'll represent you!

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:49.070
They got away?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.080
She was more powerful
than we thought.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.250
We could've seriously gotten hurt.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:01.610
We've caught you
using magic red-handed.

00:22:01.610 --> 00:22:03.090
Accompany us to the station.

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:06.330
That wasn't us!

00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:08.150
What about that diaboloid?

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:09.650
...That's mine...

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:32.940
My heart may cry silently,

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:32.940
kokoro ga donna ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:40.500
but I still want to behold the blue sky

00:22:33.340 --> 00:22:40.500
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:48.070
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.740 --> 00:22:48.070
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:55.470
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:55.470
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.470 --> 00:23:02.900
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.470 --> 00:23:02.900
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:06.740
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:06.740
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:15.180
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:15.180
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:20.400
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:20.400
kono mune no hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:22.450
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:22.450
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:29.820
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.450 --> 00:23:29.820
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:37.910
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:37.910
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
